Chapter: GptHdrCrcGuardTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Gpt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The negative control for gpt-header-crc-ok. The .disk sidecar is the valid
 gop-fat16 image with ONE change: a byte of the DiskGUID at header offset 56 is
 flipped. Nothing in this chapter reads that field, so the signature, the entry
 LBA, the count and the size are all still correct and the volume is otherwise
 exactly the one the positive arm mounts. The ONLY thing that can object is the
 header CRC, which is what makes this an integrity arm and not a parsing one.

 Ablate gpt-header-crc-ok and this flips to esp-start=64 stage=7: the table is
 accepted and the ESP start LBA it carries is handed out unchallenged.

Section: Main

  show-esp : [Device.Port] Text
  show-esp = act
    s <- gpt-esp-start
    "esp-start=" & show s & " stage=" & show (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    a <- show-esp
    print-line-uni a
  end
